<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 75.7 trln lira of 6-mth bills.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 75.7 trln lira of 6-mth bills.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish treasury sold 75.73 trillion lira of six-month discount bills in an auction on Tuesday. The previous six-month t-bill auction was on November 19, 1996.</p>
<p>    Amount	 : 75.73 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Total bids   : 153.02 trillion lira</p>
<p>     Maximum yield: 119.41 percent</p>
<p>     Maturity     : December 24, 1997</p>
<p>    Value date   : June 25, 1997</p>
<p>Banks will pay 50.6 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday when the central bank will inject 24.6 trillion lira to the banks for maturing open market reverse repo deals.</p>
<p>The central bank has issued two-year, inflation-indexed bonds in the past seven auctions held since the beginning of April.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
